## Authorized cohort and timing

- Harbor Health and Mosaic Commerce are the only accounts authorized for this pilot.
- The pilot is read-only and runs for 30 days beginning March 10, 2025.
- Customer access remains closed until March 10. Access for every other customer remains closed.

## Required lookup path and permitted output

- Every lookup must use the shared authorization wrapper.
- Permitted output is limited to provenance-backed deploy events, published service ownership, incident-load summaries with source timestamps, and explicit unknown states when data is absent.

## Automatic technical stop conditions

Immediately suspend all pilot access for any of the following:

- authorization-wrapper bypass;
- any adapter call after a denial;
- any cross-tenant material;
- any stale or missing source rendered as something other than explicit unknown;
- any deploy event without required provenance;
- any unpublished ownership;
- any incident-load summary without its source timestamp;
- exposure of raw incident text;
- exposure of internal room metadata;
- individual comparisons;
- inferred ownership;
- fallback to internal-only metadata;
- loss of read-only enforcement.

After a stop, access remains suspended until the issue is corrected and the affected safety check reruns successfully. Latency and other error signals remain monitored but are not independent automatic stops unless they cause one of the listed violations.

# Lantern customer access renewal — March 25, 2027

## Final decision
The March 25 continuation review is complete. Hema and Theo authorized Harbor Health and Mosaic Commerce, and no other account, to continue with bounded read-only Lantern access from April 1 through September 30, 2027.

## Effective-date boundary
The existing authorization remains unchanged through March 31, 2027. The renewed term begins April 1 and does not take effect early.

## Authorized lookup path and read-only surface
Every Harbor Health and Mosaic Commerce lookup remains behind the shared authorization wrapper. The permitted customer surface is limited to:
- provenance-backed deploy movement;
- published service ownership;
- timestamped incident-load summaries; and
- explicit unknown states.

## Complete exclusions
The renewed term does not authorize:
- any additional customer account;
- cost data;
- CSV export;
- raw incident text;
- internal room metadata;
- employee identifiers or comparisons;
- inferred or unpublished ownership;
- internal-only fallback data;
- write capability or writeback;
- release-readiness judgments;
- employee-performance interpretations; or
- customer exposure of the internal owner-map/Cardinality Guardrails reference navigation.

## Internal reference-only integration
The owner-map/Cardinality Guardrails reference-only integration remains an internal navigation mechanism and stays outside the Harbor Health and Mosaic Commerce customer surface. It is not included in this renewal.

## Automatic suspension conditions
Either of the following violations immediately suspends both accounts pending correction and a successful rerun of the affected safety check:
- an authorization-wrapper bypass;
- an adapter call after denial;
- cross-tenant material;
- stale or missing input rendered as anything other than explicit unknown;
- a deploy event without required provenance;
- unpublished ownership;
- an incident-load summary without its source timestamp;
- exposure of any excluded field; or
- loss of read-only enforcement.

Latency and other errors do not independently suspend access unless they cause one of the listed violations.

## Term close
This record governs the Harbor Health and Mosaic Commerce authorization through September 30, 2027. It grants no access to any other account and does not expand the authorized data or capability surface.
